==Trivia==
*Teacher A's Japanese name, Kōkō Kyōshi (高校教師, "High School Teacher"), is a possible reference to the [[wikipedia:Kōkō Kyōshi|television drama]] of the same name. The main characters of ''Kōkō Kyōshi'' are Takao Hamura, a seemingly nice new teacher at an all-girls school, and his dearest student, Mayu Ninomiya; these two may be represented by Teacher A and [[Maiden Cat (Rare Cat)|Maiden Cat]] in [[Teacher! It's Spring! (Monthly Event)|Teacher! It's Spring!]]'s event poster, which describes Teacher A as a stylish rookie teacher. All the cats in [[April Gauntlet]]'s event poster have bows on their heads, implying that Teacher A works at an all-girls school like Hamura.
*In Teacher! It's Spring!'s [[Media:Eve l 004 en.png|event poster]], Teacher A is referred to as "Teacher A.", with a period at the end of his name, but in later appearances such as April Gauntlet's event poster and the [[Enemy Guide]] entry added in [[Version 13.3 Update|Version 13.3]], his name does not have a period.

